<script>
' Minimal custom loadingComponent for the router-outlet transition demo — see Shell.thr's own
' childOutlet usage and GRAMMAR.md's "Router" section. FlashTheaterRouterOutlet.brs centers
' whatever component loadingComponent names on the outlet's own translation point
' ([width/2, height/2] — see that field's own doc comment on FlashTheaterRouterOutlet.xml); this
' component's own root offsets itself by half its own box size so the visible box actually lands
' centered ON that point, rather than with its own top-left corner there. A plain custom .thr
' component works exactly like Roku's built-in "BusySpinner" for this purpose —
' loadingComponent accepts either, see GRAMMAR.md.
</script>
<component>
<Rectangle id="root" color="0x2A2A2AFF" width="240" height="64" translation="[-120, -32]">
  <Label id="label" text="Loading..." color="0xFFFFFFFF" horizAlign="center" vertAlign="center" width="240" height="64" />
</Rectangle>
</component>
